{*
	Translation: the {_} tag, the {translate} block and the |translate filter.
	Nothing in this file may be underlined.

	The three of them are one feature in Latte 2.11 and a separate extension in
	Latte 3, where nothing registers them unless the project does - nette/latte
	ships TranslatorExtension but Engine does not add it. Whichever line a
	project is on, an unregistered name here fails at render time and not at
	compile time, so the plugin has nothing to prove and must stay quiet.
*}
{var $count = 3}
{var $name = 'Example'}

<p>{_'Welcome'}</p>
<p>{_'Welcome, %s', $name}</p>
<p>{_$name}</p>
<p>{_'One item', $count}</p>

{translate}
	<p>A whole block handed to the translator.</p>
{/translate}

{translate 'domain'}
	<p>The same, with a parameter.</p>
{/translate}

<p>{$name|translate}</p>
<p>{'Welcome'|translate}</p>
<p n:translate>An element translated by the attribute form.</p>
